# Milestone 4 Lesson Overviews

## Lesson 7: Exploring Data in AI

#### Lesson 7 is a **Building Knowledge** lesson. Students explore how AI systems combine everyday data to create detailed personal inferences. They will use this knowledge to inform their Safety & Privacy guidelines in Lesson 8.

### 📝 **Lesson Overview**
<p style="font-size: 18px; font-weight: bold; background-color: #F5F7F8; padding: 10px; border-left: 5px solid #8148B2; display: inline-block; width: 100%">
<a href="https://studio.code.org/courses/aid-thinking-critically-about-ai-2025/units/1/lessons/7" target="blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
Access Lesson 7: Exploring Data in AI
</a>
</p>

<!-- Warm Up -->
<details style="background-color: #ececec; padding: 12px; margin-top: 15px; margin-bottom: 15px; border-radius: 6px;">
<summary style="font-size: 13pt; font-weight: bold;">
Warm Up (10 minutes)
</summary>
<div style="margin-top: 12px; font-size: 13pt; line-height: 1.4;">
<p style="font-size: 13pt">
Students analyze the “Z-Tech selfie” scenario to determine how small background details could reveal a home location.
</p>
<p style="font-size: 13pt">
Through discussion, students recognize how public details can combine into private or sensitive insights through inference and pattern recognition.
</p>
</div>
</details>

<!-- Activity -->
<details style="background-color: #ececec; padding: 12px; margin-bottom: 15px; border-radius: 6px;">
<summary style="font-size: 13pt; font-weight: bold;">
Activity (25 minutes)
</summary>
<div style="margin-top: 12px; font-size: 13pt; line-height: 1.4;">
<p style="font-size: 14pt"><b>🔎 Data Exploration Stations</b></p>

<div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 15px; width: 100%; margin: 15px auto;">

<div style="background-color: #F5F7F8; padding: 18px; border-radius: 12px; text-align: center;">
<img src="https://images.code.org/4078d7e393bf5ca7e50a0947a504dc24-image-1773183450291.png" alt="" style="width: 60px; height: auto; margin-bottom: 10px;">
<p style="font-size: 14pt; font-weight: bold; margin: 0 0 8px 0;">
Smart Cart Data
</p>
<p style="font-size: 12pt; margin: 0; line-height: 1.4;">
How does AI use shopping data to make inferences?
</p>
</div>

<div style="background-color: #F5F7F8; padding: 18px; border-radius: 12px; text-align: center;">
<img src="https://images.code.org/42fa684dcc7e0add704b099325bc54cf-image-1773183448233.png" alt="" style="width: 60px; height: auto; margin-bottom: 10px;">
<p style="font-size: 14pt; font-weight: bold; margin: 0 0 8px 0;">
Public Profile Safety
</p>
<p style="font-size: 12pt; margin: 0; line-height: 1.4;">
How much can AI infer from public profile data?
</p>
</div>

<div style="background-color: #F5F7F8; padding: 18px; border-radius: 12px; text-align: center;">
<img src="https://images.code.org/dbb62aae62ac4e3985a544bba169a06f-image-1773183446382.png" alt="" style="width: 60px; height: auto; margin-bottom: 10px;">
<p style="font-size: 14pt; font-weight: bold; margin: 0 0 8px 0;">
Safer Social Media
</p>
<p style="font-size: 12pt; margin: 0; line-height: 1.4;">
How can images be anonymized to reduce risk?
</p>
</div>

</div>

<p style="font-size: 13pt">
Students classify information as <strong>Public, Private, or Sensitive</strong>, test combinations of data in AI Chat, and experiment with anonymization in Sketch Lab.
</p>

<p style="font-size: 13pt">
They identify patterns that separate safe sharing from oversharing and record Red Flags and Green Flags in their Learning Logs.
</p>
</div>
</details>

<!-- Wrap Up -->
<details style="background-color: #ececec; padding: 12px; margin-bottom: 15px; border-radius: 6px;">
<summary style="font-size: 13pt; font-weight: bold;">
Wrap Up (10 minutes)
</summary>
<div style="margin-top: 12px; font-size: 13pt; line-height: 1.4;">
<p style="font-size: 13pt">
Students reflect on how much data AI needs to feel “personal” and consider the trade-offs between personalization and privacy.
</p>
</div>
</details>

### 🧾 **What to Prepare**:
* #### Print copies of each Exploration Guide and set them up as stations.
* #### Ensure students bring their Milestone 4 Learning Log and KWL Chart.
* #### Preview anonymization activities in Sketch Lab.
* #### Plan time for group discussion and synthesis.

### 💡 **Tips for Teaching**:
* #### Push students to explain why a data point belongs in a specific category.
* #### Encourage discussion about how multiple harmless details can combine into sensitive information.
* #### Reinforce that AI inference is powered by pattern recognition, not intention.
* 
___

#### **Up Next**: Preview *only* the Sketch Lab levels for Lesson 7 to get an idea of what students will create.
